  "title": "Festival Steam Kitchens",
  "rules": [
    "Each of six kitchens has four separate actors: preparer, steamer, runner and engineer. Selecting a person means selecting its original native action row.",
    "Colored counters are physical obstacles: pantry, board, pot, cooling rack, hatch, valve and sink. Turn toward a counter before interacting.",
    "Use a knife to prepare roots or beans. A clean plate and prepared ingredient enter an empty pot; tongs or a tray lift the hot meal once progress reaches 4.",
    "Carried heat falls one per tick. A zero-heat hot meal still needs the cooling-rack action before serving.",
    "Serving the requested ingredient has quality 2; a substitution has quality 1. Only workers next to the hatch can read its current menu and deadline.",
    "A served plate becomes a dirty dish cart in the lane. Push or pick it up, wash it at a sink, then return the clean plate to a pot.",
    "An open valve draws at most two steam units. Unused steam advances through two buffers to the next kitchen; valve choices change downstream timing.",
    "This source-bound kitchen scene and its literal scripts have not been run. Native animation, human play, causal effects and learning remain unverified."
  ],
